{t: On Raglan Road}
{st:  open G tuning on tenor: G B D G}

{define: G base-fret 1 frets 0 0 0 0}
{define: C base-fret 0 frets 0 1 2 0}
{define: Bm base-fret 0 frets 4 3 0 4}
{define: Em base-fret 0 frets 0 0 2 0}
{define: D base-fret 0 frets 2 1 0 2}
{define: Am base-fret 0 frets 2 1 2 2}



Verse 1:
On [G]Raglan Road on an [Bm]autumn [C]day
I [Em] saw her [D]first and [G]knew
That [C]her dark hair would [Bm]weave a [Em]snare
that [G]I might [Bm]one day [Am]rue [D]
I [C]saw the danger [Bm]yet I [Em]passed 
a [G]long the [Em]enchanted [Am]way [D]
And I [G]said "Let grief be a [Bm]falling [C]leaf
At the [Em]dawning [D]of the [G]day".

Verse 2:
On [G]Grafton Street in [Bm]Novem[C]ber
we tripped [Em]lightly a [D]long the [G]ledge
Of a [C]deep ravine where [Bm]can be [Em]seen
the [G]worth of [Em]passion's [Am]pledge [D]
The [C]Queen of Hearts still [Bm]making [Em]tarts,
and [G]I'm not [Em]making [Am]hay [D]
Oh I [G]loved too much and by [Bm]such, by [C]such
is [Em]happiness [D]thrown a [G]way.

Verse 3:
I [G]gave her gifts [Bm]of the [C]mind
I [Em]gave her the [D]secret [G] sign
That's [C]known to the [Bm]artists [Em]who have [G]known
the true [Em]gods of sound and [Am]stone [D]
And [C]word and tint and [Bm]without [Em]stint,
I [G]gave her poems to [Am]say [D]
With her [G]own name there and [Bm]own her dark [C]hair
Like the [Em]clouds over [D]fields of [G]May.


Verse 4:
On a [G]quiet street where [Bm]old ghosts [C]meet
I [Em]see her [D]walking [G]now
A [C]way from me so [Bm]hurried[Em]ly
my [G]reason [Em]must [Am]allow [D]
That [C]I have loved [Bm]not as I [Em]should
a [G]creature [Em]made of [Am]clay [D]
when the [G]angel woos the [Bm]clay he'll [C]lose
his [Em]wings at the [D]dawn of [G]day.
